VERDICT: PASS -- ECMP on the x960-56YSQ distributes traffic over two equal-cost
         static next hops in the DATAPLANE, counted per egress port on four
         independent counters across three devices. One route puts 1920 of 1920
         frames on one port; adding the second splits them; `maximum-paths 1`
         collapses the identical flow set back onto a single port as the guide says
         it must; removing a next hop returns all traffic to the survivor; and the
         configuration survives a real reboot.
